            <ArticleTitle>Eptifibatide does not influence lymphocyte activation and CRP levels in patients with undergoing coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>107-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inhibitors of the IIB-IIIA integrin are widely used to prevent stent thrombosis. Abciximab has been shown to attenuate the inflammatory response in patients undergoing PCI. Herein, we tested the effect of eptifibatide infused during PCI on peripheral lymphocyte activation and CRP levels before, and one month after the procedure showing no noticeable effect. These results may explain the differences in clinical outcome following PCI by use of different IIB-IIIA agents.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
